The binding added, in `crates/nmp-nip60/src/nutzap.rs::verify_nutzap_dleq_against_keyset`, right after the existing missing-DLEQ/missing-`r` checks and before the mint pubkey lookup:

```rust
// Bind to the proof's claimed keyset (#2963, mirrors `blinded.rs`).
if proof.id != keyset.id {
    return Err(Nip60Error::Crypto(format!(
        "nutzap proof (C={}) claims keyset {}, expected {}",
        proof.c, proof.id, keyset.id
    )));
}
```

This mirrors `blinded.rs`'s `sig.id != keyset.id` guard on the mint/swap path and fails closed before `pubkey_map.get(&proof.amount)` is ever consulted. [...] What happened on the trim: when I went to push my condensation, the branch had already advanced — a trim (`eff514dc0`, "condense module doc to clear the 500-LOC hard cap") was already pushed, bringing nutzap.rs to 487 LOC. Rather than force-push my redundant alternative, I discarded my local commit and reset to that head. Verified on it:
- Guard intact (`proof.id != keyset.id` at nutzap.rs:380), logic and tests untouched.
